### PhpDocParser::parse()

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpdoc-parser/blob/2.3.x/_autodocs/api-reference-parser.md

Parses a complete PHPDoc comment string into a PhpDocNode AST structure.

```APIDOC
## PhpDocParser::parse()

### Description
Parses a complete PHPDoc comment into a `PhpDocNode` object. This method requires a `TokenIterator` generated by the lexer.

### Signature
`public function parse(TokenIterator $tokens): Ast\PhpDoc\PhpDocNode`

### Parameters
- **$tokens** (TokenIterator) - Required - The token stream obtained from `Lexer::tokenize()`.

### Returns
- **PhpDocNode** - The root AST node containing all PHPDoc children, including tags and text.

### Throws
- **ParserException** - Thrown if the provided PHPDoc syntax is invalid.

### Example
```php
$config = new ParserConfig(usedAttributes: []);
$lexer = new Lexer($config);
$constExprParser = new ConstExprParser($config);
$typeParser = new TypeParser($config, $constExprParser);
$phpDocParser = new PhpDocParser($config, $typeParser, $constExprParser);

$tokens = new TokenIterator($lexer->tokenize('/** @param string $x @return int */'));
$phpDocNode = $phpDocParser->parse($tokens);
```
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Node Attributes

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpdoc-parser/blob/2.3.x/README.md

Enable tracking of line numbers, token indexes, and comments using ParserConfig.

```php
$config = new ParserConfig(usedAttributes: ['lines' => true, 'indexes' => true, 'comments' => true]);
```

--------------------------------

### Parse PHPDoc string

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpdoc-parser/blob/2.3.x/CLAUDE.md

Initializes the parser components and parses a simple PHPDoc string into an AST.

```php
$config = new ParserConfig(usedAttributes: []);
$lexer = new Lexer($config);
$constExprParser = new ConstExprParser($config);
$typeParser = new TypeParser($config, $constExprParser);
$phpDocParser = new PhpDocParser($config, $typeParser, $constExprParser);

$tokens = new TokenIterator($lexer->tokenize('/** @param Lorem $a */'));
$phpDocNode = $phpDocParser->parse($tokens);
```

